01:12:33,340 --> 01:12:34,300
Aim camera.

1096
01:12:53,200 --> 01:12:54,600
And... Oh!

1097
01:12:55,780 --> 01:12:56,300
Oh!

1098
01:12:57,760 --> 01:12:58,280
Yeah!

1099
01:12:59,260 --> 01:13:00,280
Docked, baby!

1100
01:13:01,020 --> 01:13:01,700
Mission complete.

1101
01:13:02,380 --> 01:13:02,920
Okay, good.

1102
01:13:03,380 --> 01:13:08,520
Now we can disengage, but I'm also gonna... Let me see here.

1103
01:13:12,380 --> 01:13:13,820
How would I... wait, how do I do this?

1104
01:13:15,080 --> 01:13:16,480
This is one vessel now, right?

1105
01:13:16,820 --> 01:13:18,800
Oh, wait, we can... Ah!

1106
01:13:19,060 --> 01:13:19,380
Okay.

1107
01:13:20,220 --> 01:13:23,100
So, Bob, you're coming back.

1108
01:13:23,360 --> 01:13:24,800
I need all the scientists I can get.

1109
01:13:25,440 --> 01:13:28,260
Then again, having a scientist on this makes sense, though, right?

1110
01:13:30,020 --> 01:13:31,660
Maybe I'll bring one of the new guys in there, then.

1111
01:13:33,080 --> 01:13:34,360
Yeah, do a little rotation.

1112
01:13:35,160 --> 01:13:37,140
And then we can bring back Jebediah.

1113
01:13:37,720 --> 01:13:39,920
Because I have plans for Jebediah today, guys.

1114
01:13:40,760 --> 01:13:42,580
Jebediah is gonna go on an adventure.

1115
01:13:44,120 --> 01:13:44,840
Uh, it's full.

1116
01:13:44,960 --> 01:13:45,900
Okay, so let's go on the other one.

1117
01:13:50,800 --> 01:13:51,320
Here.

1118
01:13:51,320 --> 01:13:52,080
There you go.

1119
01:13:52,340 --> 01:13:52,980
He's inside.

1120
01:13:53,500 --> 01:13:57,260
Alright, let's grab... Nah, ravioli I like.

1121
01:13:58,540 --> 01:14:06,100
Samwin... Samwin, you get to... Nah, ravioli... You get to stay on this station.

1122
01:14:07,560 --> 01:14:08,940
Someone's gotta make food, you know?

1123
01:14:09,180 --> 01:14:10,280
And it has to be you.

1124
01:14:12,480 --> 01:14:13,260
In you go.

1125
01:14:13,760 --> 01:14:16,780
And then we bring... Frickin' Jebediah, man!

1126
01:14:18,210 --> 01:14:19,630
Jebediah's gonna come back home.

1127
01:14:20,410 --> 01:14:21,890
Because we've got plans for him.

1128
01:14:25,310 --> 01:14:26,790
And I guess he's gonna go in here.

1129
01:14:29,130 --> 01:14:29,890
There we go.

1130
01:14:30,590 --> 01:14:32,010
Alright, time for undocking.

1131
01:14:37,560 --> 01:14:38,360
How do I do that?

1132
01:14:40,620 --> 01:14:41,180
Undock.

1133
01:14:43,080 --> 01:14:43,900
Did it work?

1134
01:14:44,880 --> 01:14:46,060
Yep, it's working.

1135
01:14:46,940 --> 01:14:48,080
Very slight force there.

1136
01:14:56,460 --> 01:14:56,980
Beautiful.

1137
01:14:56,980 --> 01:14:59,320
We got Valentina, Jebediah, and Samwen.

1138
01:15:00,660 --> 01:15:01,500
And Oberyn.

1139
01:15:02,040 --> 01:15:02,560
Opedrin.

1140
01:15:03,000 --> 01:15:03,300
Sorry.

1141
01:15:03,680 --> 01:15:04,200
Opedrin.

1142
01:15:05,020 --> 01:15:06,400
Okay, let's bring him home.

1143
01:15:08,880 --> 01:15:11,480
We got 680 meters per second delta V.

1144
01:15:12,020 --> 01:15:13,040
That should be doable.

1145
01:15:14,080 --> 01:15:14,880
No problem.

1146
01:15:15,520 --> 01:15:18,500
The only problem is we're polar orbiting right now, which is not great.

1147
01:15:19,820 --> 01:15:21,640
Ideally, we want to burn over here, I guess.

1148
01:15:23,060 --> 01:15:27,240
And we want to burn... down, in this case.

1149
01:15:28,840 --> 01:15:29,960
Okay, that's not bad.

1150
01:15:32,120 --> 01:15:33,360
We can probably make that better.

1151
01:15:39,840 --> 01:15:40,980
Okay, we found a minimum.

1152
01:15:49,720 --> 01:15:50,700
That's a minimum there.

1153
01:15:54,320 --> 01:15:55,480
Let me just give it some more juice.

1154
01:16:05,660 --> 01:16:06,240
33.

1155
01:16:07,260 --> 01:16:09,100
Oh, dude, we have plenty!

1156
01:16:09,420 --> 01:16:09,980
Are you kidding me?

1157
01:16:13,500 --> 01:16:14,080
Easy.

1158
01:16:15,400 --> 01:16:16,820
We got electric charge.

1159
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:17,380
We're cooking.

1160
01:16:18,000 --> 01:16:18,500
We're cooking.

1161
01:16:19,200 --> 01:16:20,120
No problem.

1162
01:16:21,500 --> 01:16:22,340
Alright, brother.

1163
01:16:24,220 --> 01:16:25,380
Thanks for the high-five.

1164
01:16:25,660 --> 01:16:26,400
We're out of here.

1165
01:16:28,580 --> 01:16:29,320
See ya.

1166
01:16:32,810 --> 01:16:35,430
I like that we're speeding up so fast, but we're moving so slow.

1167
01:16:35,590 --> 01:16:38,630
I was expecting to go, but not really.

1168
01:16:39,270 --> 01:16:40,010
That's so funny.

1169
01:16:41,590 --> 01:16:42,830
Wait, are we gonna crash into each other?

1170
01:16:45,700 --> 01:16:48,140
Please don't scratch my paint.

1171
01:16:48,440 --> 01:16:50,060
I just had it made.

1172
01:16:50,840 --> 01:16:51,860
Brand new.

1173
01:16:53,080 --> 01:16:54,260
At the paint spray.

1174
01:16:56,060 --> 01:16:57,080
Here we go.

1175
01:16:57,360 --> 01:16:59,280
Three, two, one.

1176
01:17:00,020 --> 01:17:00,840
Bye-bye!

1177
01:17:01,660 --> 01:17:02,540
See ya!

1178
01:17:06,780 --> 01:17:07,880
Here we go.

1179
01:17:15,700 --> 01:17:16,480
Did we do it?

1180
01:17:16,660 --> 01:17:18,200
Let me see what we got here.

1181
01:17:26,980 --> 01:17:28,300
I can't trust that number.

1182
01:17:30,120 --> 01:17:30,860
Actually, I can.

1183
01:17:32,100 --> 01:17:32,920
It's a good number.

1184
01:17:36,500 --> 01:17:37,940
Look at the way the signals are bouncing.

1185
01:17:38,100 --> 01:17:38,440
It's so cool.

1186
01:17:39,720 --> 01:17:42,200
Wait, that's a very roundabout way of getting the signal back.

1187
01:17:42,200 --> 01:17:42,760
Are you kidding me?

1188
01:17:43,440 --> 01:17:44,860
Why is it going to Minmus first?

1189
01:17:45,760 --> 01:17:46,840
That makes no sense.

1190
01:17:49,160 --> 01:17:50,760
Guys, I feel so confident.

1191
01:17:51,620 --> 01:17:55,080
I almost want to disengage this part right now.

1192
01:17:55,300 --> 01:17:56,460
Even though we're all the way out here.

1193
01:17:57,520 --> 01:17:58,620
But let's not do that.

1194
01:17:58,720 --> 01:18:00,320
Let's actually play it smart for once.

1195
01:18:03,980 --> 01:18:04,900
Coming back home.

1196
01:18:09,720 --> 01:18:11,340
Don't go faster.

1197
01:18:11,840 --> 01:18:13,480
Just slow down, slow down.

1198
01:18:16,840 --> 01:18:17,700
Be patient.

1199
01:18:19,060 --> 01:18:19,920
Be patient.

1200
01:18:25,120 --> 01:18:32,880
Now, the only problem we have left, or I wouldn't call it a problem, just, you know, an untested thing, is the re-entry here with the cupola.

1201
01:18:33,600 --> 01:18:35,160
Actually, it's not a cupola, it's the other one.

1202
01:18:35,340 --> 01:18:37,340
It's a landing thingy.

1203
01:18:38,220 --> 01:18:38,840
You know what I mean.

1204
01:18:41,180 --> 01:18:42,020
Let's turn retro.

1205
01:18:43,720 --> 01:18:47,080
We're coming in at 3k meters per second.

1206
01:18:48,360 --> 01:18:49,840
Ah, on the dark side, though!

1207
01:18:51,860 --> 01:18:52,320
Hmm.

1208
01:18:52,620 --> 01:18:54,460
Guys, we could land right here if I slow down enough.

1209
01:18:55,500 --> 01:18:56,260
Is that crazy?

1210
01:19:01,810 --> 01:19:02,950
I want shallow.

1211
01:19:04,810 --> 01:19:05,890
I mean steep.

1212
01:19:06,390 --> 01:19:06,990
Steep me.

1213
01:19:07,650 --> 01:19:08,910
Steep me in sauce.

1214
01:19:10,410 --> 01:19:11,210
That is fine.

1215
01:19:11,770 --> 01:19:12,750
Let's disengage it.

1216
01:19:15,030 --> 01:19:16,050
See ya, brother.

1217
01:19:16,850 --> 01:19:17,570
Bye-bye.

1218
01:19:17,910 --> 01:19:19,770
Uh-oh.

1219
01:19:21,130 --> 01:19:22,010
What happened?

1220
01:19:26,220 --> 01:19:26,840
There we go.

1221
01:19:26,980 --> 01:19:27,420
Okay, okay, good.

1222
01:19:28,060 --> 01:19:28,320
SAS?

1223
01:19:28,600 --> 01:19:28,860
Retro.

1224
01:19:29,000 --> 01:19:29,200
Quick.

1225
01:19:30,380 --> 01:19:30,820
Alright.

1226
01:19:31,240 --> 01:19:31,960
We're coming home.

1227
01:19:33,040 --> 01:19:34,020
Got the heat shield.

1228
01:19:34,240 --> 01:19:34,720
Yes, sir.

1229
01:19:35,440 --> 01:19:36,120
Everyone's on board.

1230
01:19:36,220 --> 01:19:37,420
We've got five souls on board.

1231
01:19:38,980 --> 01:19:40,580
Gonna be a landing in the dark.

1232
01:19:49,080 --> 01:19:49,860
Starting to heat.

1233
01:20:08,610 --> 01:20:09,470
Coming in hot.

1234
01:20:18,090 --> 01:20:18,910
Fucking textbook.

1235
01:20:20,590 --> 01:20:20,990
Textbook.

1236
01:20:24,910 --> 01:20:26,150
I'm gonna be a little naughty, though.

1237
01:20:26,950 --> 01:20:29,870
I'm gonna deploy chutes quite late, so we don't have to wait too long.

1238
01:20:29,950 --> 01:20:30,890
Because we got two chutes.

1239
01:20:31,290 --> 01:20:33,710
You know, it's gonna take a while before we actually hit the water.

1240
01:20:38,230 --> 01:20:42,330
I think I'll deploy them at... 3k?

1241
01:20:43,930 --> 01:20:44,550
Wait, no.

1242
01:20:44,850 --> 01:20:45,890
I got a little scared.

1243
01:20:47,890 --> 01:20:48,890
Nah, we're fine, man.

1244
01:20:48,910 --> 01:20:49,290
We're chilling.

1245
01:20:49,410 --> 01:20:49,810
What the fuck?

1246
01:20:49,990 --> 01:20:50,530
No problem.

1247
01:20:52,630 --> 01:20:53,450
Got water.

1248
01:20:54,930 --> 01:20:55,950
Ooh, coming down fast.

1249
01:20:57,610 --> 01:21:00,010
Whoa, that looks really scary.

1250
01:21:00,630 --> 01:21:02,030
Why are we coming down that fast?

1251
01:21:04,150 --> 01:21:05,210
Alright, we should be good.

1252
01:21:06,470 --> 01:21:07,130
You know what?

1253
01:21:07,290 --> 01:21:09,210
Let me... See ya.

1254
01:21:10,190 --> 01:21:11,290
Bye-bye, heat shield.

1255
01:21:13,330 --> 01:21:14,150
Nice knowing ya.

1256
01:21:17,210 --> 01:21:17,610
Whee!

1257
01:21:20,110 --> 01:21:20,510
Sweetness.

1258
01:21:26,770 --> 01:21:28,370
And... Yeah, 8 meters per second.

1259
01:21:28,430 --> 01:21:29,710
We were at 10 meters per second before.

1260
01:21:31,670 --> 01:21:32,070
Beautiful!

1261
01:21:32,910 --> 01:21:33,830
We made it home.

1262
01:21:37,350 --> 01:21:40,670
Guys, the believers got the payout.

1263
01:21:41,970 --> 01:21:43,210
Oh, it's raining at home.

1264
01:21:46,230 --> 01:21:47,990
Let's pass forward to the next morning.

1265
01:21:48,470 --> 01:21:51,230
Okay, we will indeed rescue all three.

1266
01:21:53,330 --> 01:21:54,130
There you go.

1267
01:21:54,730 --> 01:21:55,250
Done.

1268
01:21:57,050 --> 01:21:58,350
I can't believe it.

1269
01:22:04,140 --> 01:22:04,780
Okay.

1270
01:22:04,780 --> 01:22:07,340
Now, what next?

1271
01:22:14,240 --> 01:22:15,200
Nah, man.

1272
01:22:17,040 --> 01:22:18,280
Guys, I just realized.

1273
01:22:22,260 --> 01:22:24,400
The thing is, though, we did rescue them, okay?

1274
01:22:25,120 --> 01:22:27,000
The believers were winning on that.

1275
01:22:27,840 --> 01:22:29,280
But this is some bullshit.

1276
01:22:29,440 --> 01:22:29,800
Come on!

1277
01:22:30,280 --> 01:22:30,500
Hey!

1278
01:22:30,980 --> 01:22:33,720
Let me get my... Oh, man, I didn't think about that.

1279
01:22:34,140 --> 01:22:35,380
Oh, that's annoying.

1280
01:22:36,100 --> 01:22:37,020
That's annoying.

1281
01:22:38,400 --> 01:22:42,660
Do a complex scan with a rover arm on Gilly Ridgeline.

1282
01:22:43,880 --> 01:22:47,980
Transmit 6-7% of the total available science for Gilly Ridgeline.

1283
01:22:48,460 --> 01:22:49,040
Hmm.

1284
01:22:49,720 --> 01:22:53,780
Is that a specific spot or, like, biome or... what?

1285
01:22:56,000 --> 01:22:58,320
We can't just leave vessels in orbit of Duna forever.

1286
01:23:04,580 --> 01:23:07,040
Return to Kerbin from orbit of Duna.

1287
01:23:08,240 --> 01:23:09,520
This is perfect.

1288
01:23:10,460 --> 01:23:12,240
This is exactly what I needed.

1289
01:23:12,780 --> 01:23:14,180
Also, look how rich we are.

1290
01:23:14,320 --> 01:23:15,080
Oh my god.

1291
01:23:16,520 --> 01:23:17,280
Nice.

1292
01:23:18,060 --> 01:23:19,200
Very nice.

1293
01:23:20,380 --> 01:23:24,340
Map 10 asteroids endangering Kerbin with a sentinel infrared telescope?

1294
01:23:28,980 --> 01:23:29,740
Dude!

1295
01:23:34,370 --> 01:23:36,270
Okay, we definitely got to launch a telescope.

1296
01:23:40,270 --> 01:23:43,890
Test decoupler orbiting... no, no, no thanks.

1297
01:23:45,390 --> 01:23:47,450
Test ruggedized vehicular wheel.

1298
01:23:49,090 --> 01:23:50,050
That sounds cool.

1299
01:23:51,130 --> 01:23:53,070
Finish construction of a rover on the surface of Minmus.

1300
01:23:53,150 --> 01:23:54,390
Stop with the Minmus rovers!

1301
01:23:54,870 --> 01:23:55,950
I've had enough of them.

1302
01:23:57,950 --> 01:24:00,630
Although, 533,000 for that?

1303
01:24:05,860 --> 01:24:06,820
God damn!

1304
01:24:09,040 --> 01:24:10,320
Guys, I have to do this.

1305
01:24:11,200 --> 01:24:12,640
I have to take this.

1306
01:24:13,620 --> 01:24:14,820
This amount of money?

1307
01:24:16,020 --> 01:24:17,520
For repairing a rover?

1308
01:24:19,080 --> 01:24:20,360
You gotta be shitting me.

1309
01:24:20,620 --> 01:24:22,240
Also, we need a little bit more science.

1310
01:24:22,920 --> 01:24:24,760
Actually, we should be focusing on science today.

1311
01:24:25,420 --> 01:24:27,940
Because I want to get deeper into this tech tree, you know?

1312
01:24:28,440 --> 01:24:30,720
Like, I want... I want this.

1313
01:24:32,280 --> 01:24:33,960
Very heavy rocketry, you know?

1314
01:24:34,080 --> 01:24:35,060
Like, look at all this shit.

1315
01:24:35,760 --> 01:24:36,940
That looks awesome.

1316
01:24:40,340 --> 01:24:40,840
Clydesdale.

1317
01:24:41,040 --> 01:24:42,420
Now that sounds awesome.

1318
01:24:42,900 --> 01:24:43,680
I need it.

1319
01:24:44,260 --> 01:24:45,220
How much does it cost?

1320
01:24:46,300 --> 01:24:46,800
550?

1321
01:24:51,760 --> 01:24:52,640
And this one.

1322
01:24:55,260 --> 01:24:59,580
Oh, wait, this is the one... Look at that, 800 ISP, yo!

1323
01:25:00,180 --> 01:25:00,940
Hold up.

1324
01:25:03,120 --> 01:25:04,080
I need this.

1325
01:25:04,820 --> 01:25:09,220
This sounds absolutely like batshit, doesn't it?

1326
01:25:11,500 --> 01:25:16,300
Wait a minute, don't we have some science on a space station somewhere that we can transmit right now?

1327
01:25:17,780 --> 01:25:18,620
Let's see here.

1328
01:25:20,370 --> 01:25:22,370
In fact, the space station we just docked with.

1329
01:25:23,370 --> 01:25:24,090
Where is it?

1330
01:25:25,790 --> 01:25:27,890
Oh god, I need to sort.

1331
01:25:29,570 --> 01:25:32,870
Toggle debris, ships... Oh my god, where is it?

1332
01:25:35,310 --> 01:25:36,370
Duna lander.

1333
01:25:39,170 --> 01:25:40,030
Payload rocket.

1334
01:25:42,090 --> 01:25:43,050
Am I blind?

1335
01:25:48,670 --> 01:25:50,070
Oh, it's Aldo at the bottom.

1336
01:25:51,150 --> 01:25:51,650
Whoops.

1337
01:25:53,650 --> 01:25:54,150
Okay.

1338
01:25:55,870 --> 01:25:58,610
This is where Ravioli is now, with Richdard.

1339
01:25:59,310 --> 01:26:01,310
Fucking Ravioli should be back on Curvan!

1340
01:26:03,230 --> 01:26:04,650
We got 80 signs in here.

1341
01:26:04,790 --> 01:26:05,530
Let's transmit that.

1342
01:26:06,850 --> 01:26:07,570
Not bad.

1343
01:26:09,790 --> 01:26:10,490
Hell yeah.

1344
01:26:12,110 --> 01:26:14,770
Then we need approximately 80 more.

1345
01:26:15,710 --> 01:26:16,950
We should be able to get that.

1346
01:26:21,110 --> 01:26:22,070
Very nice.

1347
01:26:22,550 --> 01:26:23,890
That sign's right there.

1348
01:26:29,750 --> 01:26:32,110
Then again, do I want to buy that?

1349
01:26:32,430 --> 01:26:33,870
Is it really needed right now?

1350
01:26:34,270 --> 01:26:36,190
I could also buy something for 160.

1351
01:26:37,810 --> 01:26:38,590
You know?

1352
01:26:39,910 --> 01:26:41,930
I could buy advanced landing.

1353
01:26:45,280 --> 01:26:47,320
Or... No, I don't care about that.

1354
01:26:49,200 --> 01:26:50,420
Precision engineering.

1355
01:26:52,660 --> 01:26:54,220
Weather analyzer.

1356
01:26:54,340 --> 01:26:54,980
I mean, come on.

1357
01:26:57,240 --> 01:26:57,920
Actuators.

1358
01:27:01,900 --> 01:27:05,380
I gotta say, I'm mostly interested in the 300 bracket right now.

1359
01:27:08,140 --> 01:27:09,880
Even this one sounds cool, you know?

1360
01:27:10,060 --> 01:27:11,600
Like, big solar panels and stuff.

1361
01:27:13,780 --> 01:27:14,180
Composites.

1362
01:27:16,580 --> 01:27:18,160
Bigger... fairings.

1363
01:27:23,220 --> 01:27:25,380
This thing is, like, super intriguing to me.

1364
01:27:29,270 --> 01:27:30,190
40 more science.

1365
01:27:30,430 --> 01:27:30,930
Is it possible?

1366
