04:26:06,360 --> 04:26:07,380
Oh shit, what's happening?

4061
04:26:08,760 --> 04:26:09,700
Aw, sunset.

4062
04:26:11,280 --> 04:26:13,180
Do a quick EVA report out here.

4063
04:26:14,140 --> 04:26:15,660
Do some quick EVA science.

4064
04:26:17,080 --> 04:26:19,080
Uh, nah, get in, get in, get in.

4065
04:26:19,420 --> 04:26:19,980
Just get in.

4066
04:26:22,680 --> 04:26:23,240
Okay.

4067
04:26:24,020 --> 04:26:24,880
Detachment time.

4068
04:26:26,740 --> 04:26:27,300
Decouple.

4069
04:26:29,320 --> 04:26:30,540
Uh, go.

4070
04:26:34,710 --> 04:26:35,670
We're coming back.

4071
04:26:55,130 --> 04:26:56,010
Hold retro.

4072
04:27:04,640 --> 04:27:05,760
3,300.

4073
04:27:10,580 --> 04:27:13,200
Oh, we are... getting some heat.

4074
04:27:15,200 --> 04:27:16,200
But it should be okay.

4075
04:27:34,280 --> 04:27:35,500
Oh, we're slowing down.

4076
04:27:40,860 --> 04:27:42,280
Things are exploding back there.

4077
04:27:48,100 --> 04:27:48,800
What's that?

4078
04:27:49,960 --> 04:27:51,440
Seafield's rescue mission, touchdown.

4079
04:27:51,680 --> 04:27:52,920
Oh, that's down there, huh?

4080
04:27:54,600 --> 04:27:55,980
Is Seafield even still with us?

4081
04:28:00,230 --> 04:28:01,490
Guys, I think that's all she wrote.

4082
04:28:02,530 --> 04:28:03,910
But we still have the parachutes.

4083
04:28:04,270 --> 04:28:05,530
They were repacked.

4084
04:28:06,170 --> 04:28:07,750
Maybe there's issues with the parachutes.

4085
04:28:07,810 --> 04:28:08,130
Who knows?

4086
04:28:08,810 --> 04:28:10,650
I've never done this where I repack them.

4087
04:28:15,140 --> 04:28:15,980
Take me down.

4088
04:28:17,860 --> 04:28:19,640
Do we go for stunts on the way down?

4089
04:28:20,300 --> 04:28:20,820
Parachuting?

4090
04:28:22,240 --> 04:28:22,760
Nah.

4091
04:28:23,080 --> 04:28:23,860
No stunts.

4092
04:28:24,360 --> 04:28:24,880
Don't do it.

4093
04:28:26,520 --> 04:28:27,800
Ooh, they look healthy!

4094
04:28:28,180 --> 04:28:28,960
Ho ho ho!

4095
04:28:30,220 --> 04:28:32,540
Let's fucking go get rid of the heat shield.

4096
04:28:33,920 --> 04:28:34,620
Oh, what?

4097
04:28:35,640 --> 04:28:36,160
Oh.

4098
04:28:36,400 --> 04:28:37,040
Well, that's awkward.

4099
04:28:37,360 --> 04:28:40,600
I guess it's gonna fall off when the parachutes actually start deploying properly.

4100
04:28:47,210 --> 04:28:49,930
Oh my god, it's so good to see the green earth.

4101
04:28:51,970 --> 04:28:52,630
Bye-bye.

4102
04:28:55,850 --> 04:28:57,470
Oh, we're flipping a little bit here.

4103
04:28:58,650 --> 04:28:59,090
Whee!

4104
04:29:00,570 --> 04:29:01,010
Whee!

4105
04:29:02,190 --> 04:29:02,630
Whee!

4106
04:29:05,050 --> 04:29:07,770
The spin is getting worse, by the way.

4107
04:29:11,340 --> 04:29:13,620
We may have to use some SAS on this.

4108
04:29:14,500 --> 04:29:17,260
Imagine we get the parachutes tangled so much that they actually snap.

4109
04:29:17,360 --> 04:29:17,580
Hold on.

4110
04:29:19,420 --> 04:29:20,320
Is that even a thing?

4111
04:29:23,500 --> 04:29:24,940
Just leave him like that, please.

4112
04:29:28,860 --> 04:29:29,300
Okay.

4113
04:29:29,640 --> 04:29:30,800
This does not look stable.

4114
04:29:31,700 --> 04:29:36,040
But of course, with the reaction wheels... Touchdown, Iron Curvin!

4115
04:29:37,360 --> 04:29:37,800
Guys!

4116
04:29:42,590 --> 04:29:43,810
Voting is cl... Oh, wait, what?

4117
04:29:44,230 --> 04:29:45,550
Oh, no, I have to click here, of course.

4118
04:29:46,590 --> 04:29:47,810
Will we land and return?

4119
04:29:48,150 --> 04:29:49,390
Yes, we will.

4120
04:29:50,910 --> 04:29:52,330
There it is, man.

4121
04:29:53,010 --> 04:29:55,210
Let's see the amount of science we came home with here.

4122
04:29:58,230 --> 04:29:58,630
Damn.

4123
04:30:06,040 --> 04:30:07,480
Was that 500-ish?

4124
04:30:07,600 --> 04:30:08,900
Oh, we have 800 science.

4125
04:30:09,320 --> 04:30:11,100
Yo, 18 XP gained.

4126
04:30:12,220 --> 04:30:14,340
Jebediah is now a real veteran.

4127
04:30:15,840 --> 04:30:17,180
That's crazy, bro.

4128
04:30:21,380 --> 04:30:22,040
Nice.

4129
04:30:22,440 --> 04:30:23,200
Nice, nice.

4130
04:30:24,260 --> 04:30:24,920
Wow.

4131
04:30:25,780 --> 04:30:26,140
Wow.

4132
04:30:27,020 --> 04:30:27,240
What?

4133
04:30:28,060 --> 04:30:29,360
Stop giving me this mission.

4134
04:30:29,580 --> 04:30:30,640
I've done it before, man.

4135
04:30:32,320 --> 04:30:32,980
No.

4136
04:30:34,410 --> 04:30:36,750
How about giving me some Duna missions?

4137
04:30:36,970 --> 04:30:38,410
Like planting a flag on Duna, perhaps?

4138
04:30:39,930 --> 04:30:42,710
See, that would have been something I... I could have done that, actually.

4139
04:30:42,770 --> 04:30:44,930
I can't believe I didn't do that while I was there.

4140
04:30:48,180 --> 04:30:49,820
Alright, well, that's it for then.

4141
04:30:50,060 --> 04:30:51,100
Or for now, I mean.

4142
04:30:51,420 --> 04:30:52,900
We actually freaking did it.

4143
04:30:54,600 --> 04:30:55,940
That is surprising to me.

4144
04:30:56,420 --> 04:30:58,340
I really did not think we were gonna make it.

4145
04:30:58,940 --> 04:31:03,240
The believers... were believing more than I was.

4146
04:31:04,180 --> 04:31:05,940
And I think the believers fueled me.

4147
04:31:08,100 --> 04:31:08,580
Wow.

4148
04:31:11,040 --> 04:31:11,520
Damn.

4149
04:31:12,440 --> 04:31:13,480
Oy, oy, oy.

4150
04:31:16,950 --> 04:31:18,910
That was such a good stream, man.

4151
04:31:20,050 --> 04:31:21,630
Four and a half hours of pure madness.

4152
04:31:24,510 --> 04:31:27,470
You can drag and mouse wheel and maneuver... Oh, yeah, I know that, actually.

4153
04:31:27,550 --> 04:31:28,910
I just don't do it for some reason.

4154
04:31:30,230 --> 04:31:31,430
I do like clicking on it, though.

4155
04:31:31,510 --> 04:31:32,230
It's very precise.

4156
04:31:36,500 --> 04:31:39,380
Almost lost a Kerbal for science and space low above Kerbin.

4157
04:31:41,480 --> 04:31:43,060
That was close, I will say that.

4158
04:31:44,540 --> 04:31:45,820
It was getting a little risky.

4159
04:31:50,010 --> 04:31:53,270
You had a perfect rocket fluid, totally scuffed, and it still worked.

4160
04:31:53,330 --> 04:31:54,030
What do you mean scuffed?

4161
04:31:54,110 --> 04:31:55,210
I think I nailed that.

4162
04:31:56,950 --> 04:31:59,390
I set out to do something and I did it, didn't I?

4163
04:32:00,330 --> 04:32:02,790
And now I've learned a bunch of things for next time.

4164
04:32:03,370 --> 04:32:05,750
For example, bring RCS.

4165
04:32:08,230 --> 04:32:09,350
Man, that was annoying.

4166
04:32:09,650 --> 04:32:11,810
Like, turning that bastard was actually the worst.

4167
04:32:12,790 --> 04:32:13,790
I can't believe it.

4168
04:32:16,060 --> 04:32:17,560
Rip the Duna orbit Kerbals?

4169
04:32:17,960 --> 04:32:18,640
What do you mean, rip?

4170
04:32:18,780 --> 04:32:19,620
They're supposed to be there.

4171
04:32:20,580 --> 04:32:21,320
That's their whole job.

4172
04:32:21,440 --> 04:32:22,280
They have a science thing there.

4173
04:32:22,360 --> 04:32:23,600
They're doing science around Duna.

4174
04:32:23,700 --> 04:32:24,160
That was the point.

4175
04:32:25,140 --> 04:32:26,260
They were never gonna come home.

4176
04:32:27,820 --> 04:32:30,820
No, they're in... Guys, they're in orbit around Duna to do science.

4177
04:32:30,960 --> 04:32:32,260
They have a science vessel and everything.

4178
04:32:38,060 --> 04:32:42,640
Honestly, that triple rescue plus docking around the moon was even more impressive than the Duna one for me.

4179
04:32:42,920 --> 04:32:43,500
Wait, really?

4180
04:32:45,320 --> 04:32:46,320
Why, Witch Slayer?

4181
04:32:46,880 --> 04:32:51,660
I'm a god at, you know, rescuing people, so that was kind of easy mode for me.

4182
04:32:52,680 --> 04:32:56,300
Definitely Duna was way harder for me, you know?

4183
04:33:02,480 --> 04:33:03,680
Do they have enough snack?

4184
04:33:03,880 --> 04:33:04,660
Oh, dude, yes.

4185
04:33:04,920 --> 04:33:06,300
They can photosynthesize, don't forget.

4186
04:33:07,320 --> 04:33:09,140
They're green little guys, you know?

4187
04:33:10,840 --> 04:33:14,820
In fact, they have a snack photosynthesizer machine.

4188
04:33:15,180 --> 04:33:17,960
Where, you know, the solar panels take the energy from the sun.

4189
04:33:18,840 --> 04:33:22,920
And, you know, that energy is then radiated inside the capsule on the kerbals.

4190
04:33:23,300 --> 04:33:28,240
And when the kerbals poop and pee, that organic material gets processed into snacks.

4191
04:33:28,850 --> 04:33:31,830
So they're essentially just eating their own poop, but it's like delicious, okay?

4192
04:33:32,130 --> 04:33:33,730
It's not disgusting as it sounds.

4193
04:33:34,350 --> 04:33:35,670
That's just the science behind it.

4194
04:33:38,430 --> 04:33:39,090
It's great.

4195
04:33:41,330 --> 04:33:41,730
Hydroponics.

4196
04:33:41,870 --> 04:33:42,010
Yeah.

4197
04:33:46,730 --> 04:33:47,990
Oh, free IVA?

4198
04:33:48,450 --> 04:33:49,790
It sounds like some kind of movement.

4199
04:33:49,950 --> 04:33:51,030
Free the IVA.

4200
04:33:51,370 --> 04:33:51,910
You know?

4201
04:33:53,510 --> 04:33:55,330
Yeah, I actually forgot about that.

4202
04:33:55,410 --> 04:33:56,650
I'm gonna have to take another look at it.

4203
04:33:57,790 --> 04:33:59,730
Dude, I don't know why you guys are so obsessed with that.

4204
04:34:00,350 --> 04:34:01,950
Like, to me, it's not even that exciting.

4205
04:34:02,550 --> 04:34:04,730
Like, just the concept behind it.

4206
04:34:05,430 --> 04:34:08,190
Like, I tried it briefly, and it just seemed so incredibly janky.

4207
04:34:08,370 --> 04:34:09,030
Like, it was horrible.

4208
04:34:11,290 --> 04:34:13,610
I'm not even excited to give it another shot, honestly.

4209
04:34:15,250 --> 04:34:21,030
It's just that I never expected you would do a 90-degree inclination change and then rendezvous with RCS and dock and return.

4210
04:34:21,970 --> 04:34:25,450
Yeah, and we did the orbital... What was it?

4211
04:34:28,060 --> 04:34:28,460
Reverse?

4212
04:34:28,460 --> 04:34:29,460
Wait, how was it?

4213
04:34:29,540 --> 04:34:30,840
Orbital reverse maneuver?

4214
04:34:31,160 --> 04:34:31,560
The ORM.

4215
04:34:32,460 --> 04:34:37,840
Yeah, the fact that we went the wrong way as well was not great, so we had to do a little fun maneuver there.

4216
04:34:38,060 --> 04:34:38,700
The ORM.

4217
04:34:44,340 --> 04:34:45,740
It's awesome on big stations.

4218
04:34:45,940 --> 04:34:46,820
Okay, okay.

4219
04:34:47,760 --> 04:34:49,400
I'll try and remember for next time, okay?

4220
04:34:50,260 --> 04:34:54,420
I just don't feel like I need it in a way, but I'm gonna try it again.

4221
04:34:58,840 --> 04:35:00,740
Like, the controls of it were just really janky.

4222
04:35:01,720 --> 04:35:02,420
In my opinion.

4223
04:35:02,820 --> 04:35:04,160
But I guess I can just fix that.

4224
04:35:06,560 --> 04:35:08,340
Oh, it was Opposite Rendezvous Maneuver.

4225
04:35:08,400 --> 04:35:09,140
Yeah, I think you're right.

4226
04:35:10,140 --> 04:35:11,680
I forgot my own acronym.

4227
04:35:14,600 --> 04:35:15,460
Thank you, Witch Slayer.

4228
04:35:15,560 --> 04:35:16,300
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

4229
04:35:25,020 --> 04:35:27,080
Since GTA is cancelled, do you know what game is next?

4230
04:35:27,520 --> 04:35:29,220
I have an idea for something I want to do.

4231
04:35:29,700 --> 04:35:31,560
You'll find out within the next week, okay?

4232
04:35:32,080 --> 04:35:34,380
Within seven days, probably, you'll see something on my channel.

4233
04:35:35,280 --> 04:35:37,240
But we're still going to play Grand Theft Auto 6.

4234
04:35:37,600 --> 04:35:38,460
I'm going to say it again.

4235
04:35:38,540 --> 04:35:39,580
I said it at the start of the stream.

4236
04:35:39,800 --> 04:35:45,540
But my plan now is to get the ultimate experience playing Grand Theft Auto 6.

4237
04:35:45,920 --> 04:35:50,180
Meaning we turn on all the music, all the radio stations, everything gets on.

4238
04:35:50,660 --> 04:35:54,300
And we're gonna play it on PC with like 120 frames when it comes out.

4239
04:35:54,520 --> 04:35:57,920
It's gonna be the ultimate experience, and I'm not gonna, you know, compromise anything.

4240
04:35:58,520 --> 04:36:00,580
And I'm gonna get those VODs out there somehow.

4241
04:36:00,840 --> 04:36:02,540
If it's YouTube or not, I don't care.

4242
04:36:02,780 --> 04:36:03,740
We're gonna get them out.

4243
04:36:04,420 --> 04:36:04,820
Somehow.

4244
04:36:05,180 --> 04:36:06,520
Maybe on Patreon or something.

4245
04:36:08,460 --> 04:36:13,260
But I'm gonna get my experience, you know, with all the frames and all the music.

4246
04:36:14,040 --> 04:36:15,140
And I can't wait, man.

4247
04:36:15,260 --> 04:36:18,260
Like, I am actually pining right now for more Grand Theft Auto.

4248
04:36:18,830 --> 04:36:21,650
But I think it's better if I wait and get the ultimate experience.

4249
04:36:22,610 --> 04:36:25,790
Because I will say, man, the 30 frames is rough.

4250
04:36:26,630 --> 04:36:29,130
Especially when you go back into even this game, you know?

4251
04:36:29,690 --> 04:36:33,290
This game is running at like 100 frames for me, and it's just like night and day.

4252
04:36:34,510 --> 04:36:43,050
I don't know if you guys noticed, but in Grand Theft Auto 6, if you open the map on console, trying to actually target some of those markers is difficult.

4253
04:36:43,930 --> 04:36:46,950
Because there is so much input lag with 30 frames.

4254
04:36:47,850 --> 04:36:50,590
It's wild how bad the controls are in the map.

4255
04:36:52,270 --> 04:36:56,110
It's less bad, you know, when you're driving and stuff, but you can still really feel it.

4256
04:36:56,290 --> 04:36:57,370
I'm very sensitive to that.

4257
04:37:01,310 --> 04:37:03,210
Apparently, Grand Theft Auto 6 got cracked.

4258
04:37:05,010 --> 04:37:07,190
Is that confirmed, though, or is it just hearsay?

4259
04:37:08,090 --> 04:37:09,950
Because a lot of people are just talking shit, you know?

4260
04:37:11,170 --> 04:37:15,130
They're probably gonna try and push a coin on you guys or something.

4261
04:37:23,140 --> 04:37:25,180
About the control from here option not being there.

4262
04:37:25,400 --> 04:37:26,500
It is there only on flight.

4263
04:37:26,620 --> 04:37:27,100
Yeah, I noticed.

4264
04:37:27,700 --> 04:37:33,720
In VAB, you have to use reroute to change route part of the rocket and along with it original... Oh, okay.

4265
04:37:34,540 --> 04:37:39,920
So it's just a little more complicated to do that in the VAB compared to just flying.

4266
04:37:40,920 --> 04:37:42,100
Okay, okay, I see.

4267
04:37:47,130 --> 04:37:48,650
Oh, next time, SkyEye?

4268
04:37:48,730 --> 04:37:49,190
Let me think.

4269
04:37:51,090 --> 04:37:53,450
Next time, we're gonna be spending some science.

4270
04:37:54,490 --> 04:37:57,350
And I'm gonna be buying some really cool tech, I think.

4271
04:37:57,670 --> 04:37:59,110
And then we'll see what to do with that.

4272
04:37:59,190 --> 04:38:05,790
Maybe I'll try this telescope thing with the... with the infrared telescope stuff.

4273
04:38:06,450 --> 04:38:07,290
That could be cool.

4274
04:38:11,780 --> 04:38:12,780
Oh, we have planes.

4275
04:38:14,980 --> 04:38:17,060
I'm honestly not interested at all in making a plane.

4276
04:38:18,020 --> 04:38:20,580
If I have nothing else to do in the game, maybe I'll give it a shot.

4277
04:38:21,240 --> 04:38:23,500
Like, I have zero interest in making a plane.

4278
04:38:25,380 --> 04:38:28,340
Like, if I want to fly a plane, I'll play Microsoft Flight Simulator, you know?

4279
04:38:33,770 --> 04:38:35,390
But I will try it at some point.

4280
04:38:35,490 --> 04:38:37,910
It's just that I have all kinds of other things I'd rather do first.

4281
04:38:39,390 --> 04:38:40,610
You ever heard of endicopia?

4282
04:38:41,090 --> 04:38:41,490
Nope.

4283
04:38:41,690 --> 04:38:44,650
Sounds like a disease that you have in your eye.

4284
04:38:51,430 --> 04:38:53,570
My engineer heart hurts hearing that.

4285
04:38:54,090 --> 04:38:57,390
Dude, Microsoft Flight Simulator is, like, amazing for flying.

4286
04:39:05,440 --> 04:39:07,620
It's a strange game by a strange animator.

4287
04:39:07,900 --> 04:39:10,900
Well, there's nearly 400 games on my backlog, you know?

4288
04:39:12,240 --> 04:39:16,040
I feel like I should stop taking requests, actually, unless it's, like, really sick.

4289
04:39:16,660 --> 04:39:21,420
I will never be able to finish that backlog, even as it is right now.

4290
04:39:21,980 --> 04:39:22,960
It's unfinishable.

4291
04:39:24,700 --> 04:39:25,640
It's just too big.

4292
04:39:29,050 --> 04:39:31,050
Guys, maybe the plan is I play a smaller game.

4293
04:39:32,890 --> 04:39:33,570
Like now.

4294
04:39:33,790 --> 04:39:35,050
Not right now, in this moment.

4295
04:39:35,270 --> 04:39:37,770
But, you know, as the next one.

4296
04:39:38,030 --> 04:39:42,570
And then after that, we're gonna throw in a big one that you guys are gonna wanna see.

4297
04:39:45,110 --> 04:39:45,790
Actually, hold on.

4298
04:39:45,990 --> 04:39:47,530
Endicopia is already on my list, dude.

4299
04:39:48,510 --> 04:39:50,090
It's already on my backlog, so boom.

4300
04:39:50,210 --> 04:39:50,610
There it is.

4301
04:39:51,190 --> 04:39:53,070
Somebody already suggested that to me, I guess.

4302
04:39:53,490 --> 04:39:54,230
I just forgot.

4303
04:39:59,390 --> 04:40:00,850
You read the server for that website?

4304
04:40:00,850 --> 04:40:01,250
I do.

4305
04:40:01,510 --> 04:40:02,570
But it's very, very cheap.

4306
04:40:05,650 --> 04:40:07,090
Well, actually, the server is free.

4307
04:40:08,410 --> 04:40:10,430
But the domain name costs money.

4308
04:40:10,570 --> 04:40:12,090
And it's like 10 bucks per year or so.

4309
04:40:13,150 --> 04:40:14,550
Maybe like 9 bucks, I think.

4310
04:40:18,110 --> 04:40:19,410
Yeah, the hosting is free, I guess.

4311
04:40:20,970 --> 04:40:22,470
